text+='''
For the Daphnia–Metschnikowia scenario, the control dye assay gives a viability
lifetime of about 17.20 days, while contact with hosts at 160/L reduces the
modelled searching residence to 1.24 days and gives death share d=0.0721.
The measured infected-host lifespan is 15.78 days (these are different hosts from
the threshold experiment). These values motivate measuring infectivity decay,
filtering and successful infection in the same clone before setting a schedule.
For Holospora, total-host trajectories and dispersal are already measurable, but
free-stage loss and the horizontal/vertical balance are not calibrated here.
For phage, the assumed 0.35/0.03-day clocks remain illustrative, and dilution
removes free phage as well as hosts. No candidate is certified as a decisive test.

New repository leads were recorded after analysis began. They were screened for
future calibration and were not added to the registered inferential sample.
'''
text=text.replace('`../.. /notes/decisive-experiment-v2.md` (actual path: `../../notes/decisive-experiment-v2.md`)','`../../notes/decisive-experiment-v2.md`')
(P/'systems.md').write_text(text)
